      "what_must_be_true": "Post-emergence Wolfspeed must convert its vertically integrated 200mm footprint into utilization-driven gross-margin recovery while AI-datacenter and 800V auto demand materialize fast enough to offset legacy 150mm runoff; the refinanced ~$145M cash-interest load and near-zero net capex must hold so the ~$1.1B liquidity pool bridges to positive EBITDA around FY29 without another restructuring."
    },
    "preview_note": "WOLF's first post-emergence June quarter should land near guidance: we model revenue of ~$151M (guide $140-160M), a GAAP gross loss of ~$34M (non-GAAP margin still negative but improving from -21%), and flat opex per management's script. The GAAP net loss optically widens to ~$135M (-$2.79) because Q3's one-off $28.7M derivative fair-value gain and $10M contingent-cash gain don't repeat, while interest expense steps down to ~$40M on the March refinancing. Non-GAAP EPS of ~-$2.28 on a bigger ~48.5M share count screens better than Q3's -$3.26. Three things matter: (1) cash — Q3 burn was $84M CFO with only $5M net capex; a print near -$75M CFO and cash+ST investments >$1.0B keeps the balance-sheet story intact; (2) the mix shift — AI datacenter (+30% QoQ in Q3) and Power Products stability versus continued materials runoff; (3) the FY1Q27 guide — we expect $145-165M revenue with 'gross margin remains negative, opex flat' language. Reaction hinges less on the P&L loss than on burn trajectory and any quantified margin-inflection timeline for Mohawk Valley utilization; a sub-$140M guide or accelerating burn would reopen dilution fears despite the 2030/2031 maturity runway.",
    "reasoning": "Anchored on the Q3 FY26 8-K (0000895419-26-000024): revenue $150.2M, gross loss -$40M, opex $74.3M, interest $52.1M, non-op income -$46.2M (incl. one-off +$28.7M derivative gain and +$10M contingent cash), net loss -$119.9M, non-GAAP net loss $(128.2)M, adj EBITDA $(61.7)M, CFO -$83.8M, FCF $(90.0)M, cash $695.1M plus $469.7M ST investments. Q4 guide: revenue $140-160M, negative non-GAAP GM, flat opex. I take revenue at 151 (Q3 hit midpoint; AI datacenter momentum offsets auto softness). Gross loss narrows on Durham consolidation and lower restructuring-in-COGS. Interest drops to ~$40M reflecting the $62M annualized reduction (partially offset by the June 1L step-up). Non-op reverts to ~-$12M (interest income only), so GAAP net loss widens to -$135.3M; shares 48.5M (48.34M outstanding May 1 plus vesting) give -$2.79 GAAP, -$2.28 non-GAAP after +$24.5M adjustments (SBC 10, restructuring 6, project 5, debt-cost amortization 4, disposal -0.5). Cash flow: CFO -$75M (lower cash interest, ITC/working-capital inflows), gross capex -$30M with +$20M reimbursements/ST-investment flows in other investing, CFF -$5M; cash ends $605M. FY27 models gradual recovery (~$684M revenue, gross loss shrinking to near breakeven by Q4), heavy but narrowing burn; FY28-29 assume 200mm/AI ramp lifts revenue to ~$820M/$1,000M, gross profit positive, with a ~$300M capital raise in FY28 to sustain liquidity. Balance sheet rolls: accumulated deficit -405.8, equity 896.4, liabilities ~2,119.6 (PIK accretion offset by payables runoff)."
